  "storage": "Four fixture observations, including successful shadow/ancestor attacks as negative controls. Original cleanup receipt retained; follow-up proves exact private root removal.",
  "private_input": "Seven preamble cases plus real existing parser/reader, mapped waiter/descriptor/exec-tail checks. Pipe/process composition only; not native desktop/engine attach qualification.",
  "network": "Final inside-container and bounded-host setup variants pass with separate private peer positive/deny/allow controls and actual kernel table observation. First two failed fixture attempts retained; final private containers/image/store removed.",
  "engine": "Podman4.9.3/crun1.14.1 on WSL2, raw private exact UID0 fixture; not the supported production mapped cohort or both-profile acceptance.",
  "source_format": "Source archives keep an added .txt suffix so documentation does not create Go packages or executable test suites. Restore original names only in a fresh replay directory.",
  "image_projection": "22 layered immutable-image metadata cases pass using the actual D archive binding. Root aliases, hardlinks and type replacement included; the earlier 17-case receipt remains. This is not the bounded production parser, build-lock integration or actual engine mount observation.",
  "startup_status": "Selected reserved-fd refinement: five host and five raw isolated rootless Podman cases pass with source fd4/fd64, raw-only six-call-site compiled tail and no private descriptor leaks. Source-fd3 branch and full production qualification remain gates. Original failed fixture and incomplete cleanup receipts remain; exact cleanup follow-up proves no private root/process remains. Historical whole-range CLOEXEC proofs are not the selected kernel requirement."
